erson_id":"tvfy_10841","person_slug":"nick-mckim","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Nita Green","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10950","person_slug":"nita-green","vote":"no"},{"name":"Patrick Dodson","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10846","person_slug":"patrick-dodson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Paul Scarr","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10949","person_slug":"paul-scarr","vote":"no"},{"name":"Penny Allman-Payne","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11002","person_slug":"penny-allman-payne","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Raff Ciccone","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10915","person_slug":"raff-ciccone","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tammy Tyrrell","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_11012","person_slug":"tammy-tyrrell","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"no"}],"name":"National Anti-Corruption Commission Bill 2022 and another - in Committee - Pork barrelling and corruption definition","noes":28,"question":"The majority voted against [amendments (2) and (3) on sheet 1730](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2022-11-29.4.2) introduced by NSW Senator [David Shoebridge](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/nsw/david_shoebridge) (Greens), which means they failed. ### What do the amendments do? Regarding amendment (2), Senator Shoebridge [explained that](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2022-11-29.49.1): > *Amendment (2) seeks to re-insert a provision that was stripped out by the other place in relation to the definition of 'corruption' found in section 8 of the bill.* Regarding amendment (3), he [explained that](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2022-11-29.52.1): > *our amendment (3) is simply to put in a notation to the definition of corruption that provides, by way of guidance, that corrupt conduct may include conduct that constitutes pork-barrelling or political donations for the purpose of influencing a decision or policy made by a public official.* ### Amendment text > *(2) Clause 8, page 15 (line 20), at the end of subclause (1), add:* > >> *; (e) any conduct of a public official in that capacity that constitutes, involves or is engaged in for the purpose of corruption of any other kind.* > > *(3) Clause 8, page 15 (after line 20), at the end of subclause (1), add:* > >> *Note: Corrupt conduct may include conduct that constitutes pork barrelling or political donations for the purpose of influencing a decision or policy made by a public official.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-7890","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2022-11-29/3"}
